{
  "case_id": "2016-16-149",
  "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ESTRADA: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The issue in this case is whether FEHBA preempts State laws that forbid subrogation by insurance carriers. The Missouri Supreme Court upheld the State rule, but we believe that is wrong for at least three reasons. Number one, antisubrogation laws relate to benefits and coverage, as this Court concluded in FMC v. Holliday, and at the very least, they relate to payments with respect to benefits. Number two, if there's any ambiguity on this point, OPM's notice-and-comment regulation answers a question in favor of preemption. And number three, although the majority of the Supreme Court of Missouri thought otherwise, we believe there's no constitutional infirmity in"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Tripp)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Right. So -- so I think we would win this case even without Chevron deference, without the regulations. I think we just have the better of the two readings of the statute. The application of the presumption against preemption here, I think, is really just fundamentally misguided. Not only do we have an express-preemption provision, we're talking about Federal benefits for Federal employees under Federal contracts entered into under a Federal statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Tripp)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "if Missouri can prohibit subrogation, then what happens is that Federal workers in Illinois who are enrolled in the same plan and paying the same premiums are footing the bill for benefit payments they can't even keep, and it's not part of a State's traditional authority to impose those kinds of externalities on out-of-State Federal workers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Does the -- does the statute 8902(m)(1), does it preempt anything?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Mr. Wessler)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And Congress had a laser focus when it passed this statute in 1978. It did not want to disturb otherwise applicable State insurance laws."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Wessler, what is -- how do you differentiate our holding in Hillman?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Does your -- does your argument depend on the wording of this provision? Does it depend on the fact that it says the terms of the contract shall supersede State or local law? Would -- would you have a -- would you make the same argument if it said this statute hereby supersedes and preempts any State or local law that conflicts with the terms of the contract?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wessler",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WESSLER: I think that is -- I think that is a -- a far better approach that would -- would likely not raise these problems, because it points back to a -- a statute that actually does the preempting."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0002-0010",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Official - Subject to Final Review of this type of preemption that would actually authorize the terms of privately-negotiated contracts to step in and displace otherwise applicable sovereign decisions of States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But Congress doesn't know the term -- doesn't know what's in all these plans. They didn't know what would be in all these plans when they enacted it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wessler",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WESSLER: But the difference, Your Honor, is that here the terms are -- the terms of these contracts are determining the scope of preemption. And the terms themselves are not known by Congress at the time it passes the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wessler",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WESSLER: Well, it depends on what the statute says. And in ERISA, when Congress passed ERISA, it included a series of substantive provisions that dictate which State laws are displaced."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I think I don't quite understand your -- your answer to Justice Alito's first question. I think he gave you a statute something along the lines of this Federal law preempts and supersedes any State law that conflicts with these kinds of contracts. And you said that would not be subject to your constitutional concerns; is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-149",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c53cd22348e0d45e776db634e3e615fbf548a5790dd49b0ab2ce0468e32b008",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c53cd22348e-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel."
    },
    {
